    "body": "Untested, but I don't see why this wouldn't work\n\n<!-- Reviewable:start -->\n- - -\nThis change is [<img src=\"https://reviewable.io/review_button.svg\" height=\"34\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"Reviewable\"/>](https://reviewable.io/reviews/TokTok/c-toxcore/3071)\n<!-- Reviewable:end -->\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Not my CI issue:\n\n```\nRefusing to check out fork pull request code from a 'pull_request_target'\nworkflow. This workflow runs with the base repository's GITHUB_TOKEN,\nsecrets, default-branch cache scope, and runner access.\nFetching and executing a fork's code in that trusted context\ncommonly leads to \"pwn request\" vulnerabilities.\nTo opt in, review the risks at https://gh.io/securely-using-pull_request_target\nand set 'allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true' on the actions/checkout step.\n```",
            "created_at": "2026-08-13T03:14:06Z",
